{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>They journeyed from here.</b> There is no doubt that they journeyed from this pasture, and there is no point in searching for them in any of its parts." "<b>For I heard them saying.</b> And the reason I said that they had certainly journeyed is that I heard them saying <b>let us go</b> — not that I saw them journeying." "<b>after his brothers.</b> Even though he did not find them in Shechem as his father had said, he took on more trouble than what he was commanded, in order to attain his father's desire."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:39.157828033Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}